Chapter: GlyphUpemGuard
  cites Encode chapter TrueType
  cites Ui chapter GlyphRasterizer
  cites Ui chapter TrueTypeFont

 Track D item 19, the GlyphRasterizer leg. unitsPerEm is a raw 16-bit field of
 the head table (TrueType.codex ttf-read-head reads it with ttf-u16 and
 validates nothing), and gr-render-glyph:203 divides every outline coordinate by
 it. TWO BYTES of a font file decide whether this chapter runs.

 Measured on the unguarded chapter, both on this font with only those two bytes
 changed:

 upem = 0 kills the guest with !EXC=00, a divide error, on the first glyph
 rendered (R12 = 0x20, the space).

 upem = 1 kills it with !EXC=08, a DOUBLE FAULT, because every coordinate is
 then multiplied by ppem with no divisor to bring it back: the width came out
 0x2bc1, 11201 pixels, and w * h sized the pixel buffer.

 The font below is codex/test/truetype-bridge-test.codex's, byte for byte, with
 unitsPerEm at offsets 246 and 247 rewritten per row. Row 1 is the control and
 carries the whole arm: it is the SAME font at its real 1024, and it must still
 render 96 glyphs at 9x11, or a guard that refused everything would pass both
 hostile rows.

